2. WHAT YOU PRODUCE IS YOURS

Your input designs remain entirely yours. Seagull Work, Inc. claims no
interest in them.

Everything the program writes out is likewise yours: routed boards,
project and schematic files, gerbers, drill files, pick-and-place and
IPC-D-356 files, run verdicts, tuning files, logs. You may use, modify,
publish, fabricate, have fabricated, sell, and distribute those outputs
for any purpose, personal or commercial, with no royalty, no attribution,
and no further permission from anyone.

The example board included in this package may also be used, modified,
and redistributed freely. So may the fab library, the JSON files in the
fab/ folder: they record what each board house publishes about its own
capabilities and stackups, with the source noted in each file; Seagull
Work, Inc. claims no rights in those numbers and gives no assurance that
they are current or correct — the board house's own pages govern.

This freedom is about ownership only. It is not an assurance that any
output is correct — see sections 4 and 5, which apply to everything the
program produces.


