4. NO WARRANTY

THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS" AND "AS AVAILABLE", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF
ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES
OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, NON-INFRINGEMENT,
ACCURACY, AND QUIET ENJOYMENT.

Because this program produces designs for physical hardware, one point
deserves to be said plainly rather than left to the paragraph above:

  A run that reports zero DRC violations, zero unconnected items, and
  that every gate was met is a report from this program about its own
  work. It is not an assurance that the board is correct, routable as
  intended, manufacturable, electrically sound, thermally adequate,
  compliant with any standard or regulation, or safe.

Placement, routing, ampacity widening, impedance geometry, length
matching, stitching, and the design-rule checks reported here are
heuristics and automated checks. They can be wrong, and they can be
confidently wrong. No engineer at Seagull Work, Inc. has reviewed your
board. Before you fabricate, assemble, energize, sell, or rely on any
output of this program, review and verify it independently, by whatever
means your application warrants. Boards intended for safety-critical,
medical, automotive, aerospace, or life-support use require review
appropriate to those domains; this software is not offered as suitable
for them.

You are responsible for the engineering judgment applied to your designs.


